# RESET-clears-client-state needs CLIENT TRACKING (RESP3 client-side caching + invalidation
# push frames), which is unimplemented — a silent no-op stub would let clients believe tracking
# is active and serve them stale data, so it is deliberately absent. Phase 5 (delta item 7 / CLIENT
# TRACKING track).
RESET clears client state
# RESET-clears-authenticated-state needs the multi-user ACL engine (ACL SETUSER + AUTH <user>);
# only the default user is implemented. Phase 5, delta item 7.
RESET clears authenticated state
# "Don't rehash if redis has child process" asserts on DEBUG HTSTATS "table size:" output and
# Redis's incremental-dict rehash suppression during a save child. PeaDB uses std::unordered_map,
# which has no equivalent knob or table-size introspection.
Don't rehash if redis has child process
# proc-title-template / setproctitle is not implemented; the assertions only run on Linux (the
# test is a no-op elsewhere). Tracked as an ops-parity gap.
Process title set as expected
# FLUSHALL does not perform a foreground save that zeroes rdb_changes_since_last_save when save
# points are configured (Redis does). The dirty counter is command-granular (delta item 18), so
# the exact "== 0" assertion is out of reach; the counterpart "should not reset" test passes.
FLUSHALL should reset the dirty counter to 0 if we enable save
